#: includes/admin-page.php:1018
msgid "Why & How to Use Custom Fonts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1020
msgid "Why use custom fonts?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1020
msgid "OpenType features, such as ligatures, swashes, and stylistic sets, are built into the font files. System fonts and many web fonts have few OpenType features. Fonts from sources such as MyFonts, Adobe Fonts, or Font Squirrel often include many more."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1021
msgid "Performance benefit:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1021
msgid "By default, a font that you add here loads only on the pages that use it. If you use a decorative font on one page, it does not make the other pages on your site slower."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1022
msgid "Three ways to add fonts:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1024
msgid "Upload Font Kit:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1024
msgid "Upload a ZIP file from a font provider, such as MyFonts, Fontspring, or Google Fonts. Use this for font files that you have downloaded."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1025
msgid "Adobe Fonts:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1025
msgid "Paste the embed code from your Adobe Fonts (Typekit) project. Use this if you have an Adobe Creative Cloud subscription."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1026
msgid "Custom Font Definition:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1026
msgid "Use a font that your theme, a plugin, or a CDN already loads. Typography Stylist then shows it in the editor font list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1031
msgid "Manage the fonts that the block editor can use. Drag a font to change its position. The editor font list uses the same order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1033
msgid "Font list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1041
msgid "Add Font"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1047
#: includes/admin-page.php:1078
#: typography-stylist.php:1381
msgid "Upload Font Kit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1049
msgid "Upload a complete webfont kit as a ZIP file, for example MyWebfontsKit.zip. The ZIP can contain a CSS file and font files, or only font files (for example, a Google Fonts download). If the ZIP has no stylesheet, the plugin makes one from the metadata in the font files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1053
msgid "ZIP File:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1055
msgid "Choose ZIP file containing webfont kit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1060
msgid "Choose ZIP File"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1066
msgid "Upload a webfont kit as a ZIP file. The ZIP can contain a CSS file and font files, or only font files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1072
msgid "Clear selected file"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1085
msgid "Uploading…"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1091
msgid "How to use:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1093
msgid "Download your webfont kit from your font provider."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1094
msgid "If the kit is not a ZIP file, make a ZIP file of the whole kit folder. A CSS file is recommended, but not necessary. A ZIP of font files only also works."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1095
msgid "Click “Choose ZIP File”, then select the ZIP file of your webfont kit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1096
msgid "Click “Upload Font Kit”. The plugin reads the font names from the kit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1097
msgid "The plugin extracts the ZIP, processes the fonts, and adds them to the block editor."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1099
msgid "Compatibility Note:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1099
msgid "This plugin was tested with webfont kits from MyFonts and with font-only downloads from Google Fonts. Kits from other providers should also work. If a kit has a CSS file, the plugin uses it. For a ZIP of font files only, the plugin makes a stylesheet. The server cannot read WOFF2 metadata. For a ZIP of WOFF2 files only, the plugin gets the family and weight from the filenames. Check the result, and upload TTF files instead if something is wrong."
msgstr ""

