#: includes/admin-page.php:1586
msgid "How to Use"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1589
msgid "Method 1: Inline Format (Quick Styling)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1590
msgid "Use the inline format to style complete words or phrases in a heading, paragraph, or other text block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1592
msgid "Add or select a heading or paragraph block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1593
msgid "Select the complete words that you want to style."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1594
msgid "Click “Typography Stylist Features” in the block toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1595
msgid "Choose a preset, or turn on individual features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1596
msgid "The text changes as you work. Click “Close” when you are done."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1599
msgid "Method 2: Typography Stylist Block (Advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1600
msgid "Use the block for complex typography, for styling single letters, or when you need its built-in accessibility features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1602
msgid "Add the “Typography Stylist” block from the block inserter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1603
msgid "Choose the heading level (H1–H6) in the block toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1604
msgid "Use the sidebar controls to set the font family, size, and OpenType features for the whole block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1605
msgid "To style only part of the text, select it, then click “Typography Stylist Features” in the block toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1610
msgid "Line Breaks and the Enter Key"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1611
msgid "The Enter key works differently in a Typography Stylist block than in a regular heading or paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1613
msgid "In a Typography Stylist block:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1613
msgid "Enter adds a line break and keeps you in the same block, so a multi-line headline shares one set of typography settings. You can change this on the Options tab so Enter starts a new block instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1614
msgid "In a regular heading or paragraph:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1614
msgid "Enter ends the block and starts a new paragraph. This is standard WordPress behavior, and the plugin does not change it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1616
msgid "To add a line break in a regular heading, press Shift+Enter. If a heading has already split in two, put the cursor at the start of the paragraph below it and press Backspace. This joins the text back into the heading. Then press Shift+Enter where you want the line break."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1617
msgid "Shift+Enter also adds a line break in a Typography Stylist block, whatever the Options setting is."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1621
msgid "Choosing Fonts for OpenType Features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1622
msgid "A feature works only when the font includes it. Look for fonts with alternate glyphs and advanced OpenType features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1624
msgid "Font types that often include OpenType features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1626
msgid "Script and calligraphy fonts:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1626
msgid "Often include contextual alternates, swashes, and stylistic sets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1627
msgid "Serif display fonts:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1627
msgid "Can include titling alternates and ligatures."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1628
msgid "Professional typefaces:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1628
msgid "Many include discretionary ligatures and stylistic alternates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1629
msgid "Ornamental fonts:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1629
msgid "Can include ornaments and special character sets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1632
msgid "Add fonts on the Custom Fonts tab. You can upload a font kit, connect Adobe Fonts, or define a font that your theme or a font service already loads."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1636
msgid "Tips for Using OpenType Features"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1638
msgid "Start with contextual alternates (calt). They change letters automatically, based on the letters around them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1639
msgid "Use swashes sparingly, on first or last letters only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1640
msgid "Try the stylistic sets (ss01–ss20) to find alternate letter designs."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1641
msgid "Standard ligatures (liga) suit most text. Use discretionary ligatures (dlig) with care."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1642
msgid "Preview the text at the size it will display. Features can look different at other sizes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1643
msgid "Not every font supports every feature. Read the font’s documentation, and test each feature."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1644
msgid "To style part of a word, use the Typography Stylist block. This keeps the text accessible."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1649
msgid "Technical Notes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1650
msgid "The plugin stores features in the post content, as CSS font-feature-settings in inline styles and data attributes. It adds no database tables."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1651
msgid "All modern browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Safari, and Edge) support OpenType features."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin-page.php:1652
msgid "The pages that visitors see use only CSS. The plugin adds no JavaScript to them."
msgstr ""

